        "result":"submitted_via_eip",
        "result_type":"bool",
        "scope":"(and is_covered_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"
      },
      "local_id":"r1",
      "questions":[
        "Do any omitted provisions qualify the submission-date treatment of pending matters?",
        "Is footnote 1 exhaustive, and how are borderline communications classified?"
      ],
      "statement":"Selected control: compulsory e-IP submission route after the extended parallel run. Existing channels remain available through 29 November 2024. For each covered application or submission made from 30 November 2024, the submitter must use e-IP. Existing reporting requests are announced as integrated into e-IP, while annual-fee payment through the system remains optional. The practicability qualification concerns SFC enhancements only.",
      "subject":"Route used for an individual application or submission concerning an IPD-administered investment product"
    }
  ]
}"}}
